    "viewScroll": {
      "schema": "view-scroll-v1",
      "source": "application.ccn 04-Office. Frame header chunk 13108 (world/window). Layers chunk 13121 read as 16.16 FIXED POINT -- a float read returns 0.000 for every layer and looks like a real answer. Instances chunk 13112: 4-byte count then 20-byte records handle/oi/x/y/parentType/parentHandle/layer/unknown, instance OI is raw ^48 then ^28 for build 26. Several hitboxes are REPOSITIONED at StartOfFrame, so a placed coordinate can lie: grep the frame for SetPosition.",
      "recordedAt": "2026-09-19",
      "worldWidth": 1600,
      "worldHeight": 768,
      "windowWidth": 1024,
      "windowHeight": 768,
      "maxPanPx": 576,
      "centerDisplayFollows": "04-Office drives CenterDisplayX from an OBJECT selected by `viewing`: `camera follow 2` at viewing=0 (office), `camera follow` on some cameras, hard 0 on viewing 1-4, 5 and 6. The pan is the display centre tracking a marker, not a player-dragged offset, so that marker's x is the state variable.",
      "panDependent": {
        "hallLight": true,
        "leftVentLight": true,
        "rightVentLight": true,
        "cameraFeedLight": true,
        "mask": false,
        "monitor": "UNKNOWN"
      },
      "note": "xCoef 1.00 (layer 0) means the control scrolls 1:1 with the view, so a FIXED screen coordinate for it is only valid at a known pan offset. The light hitboxes are layer 0; the flip mask button is layer 4 at xCoef 0.00 and does not move. monitorFrame is layer 3 at xCoef 1.00 -- but that is the FRAME, and the object list does not name the monitor toggle's own hitbox, so `monitor` is UNKNOWN(not-traced) rather than assumed to scroll with it. This is why a panned office loses light presses while mask presses still land -- the asymmetry measured on Night 3, 2026-09-19. NOTHING in the executor models pan state, so every entry marked true has a coordinate valid only at pan 0.",
      "panObservation": "UNKNOWN(not-implemented): the Cue Helper reports pan_anchor_state but read UNKNOWN (pan_anchor_reason=bulb-not-found) throughout the 2026-09-19 runs.",
